<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chanyu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chanyu was the title of the supreme ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a>, roughly equivalent to emperor. The chanyu presided over a hierarchy of kings and tribal leaders and conducted relations with Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modu-chanyu">Modu Chanyu</a>, who reigned from 209 to 174 BCE, unified and organised the Xiongnu state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chanyu.jpg" alt="Chanyu" width="195" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davide Mauro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reconstruction_of_a_Xiongnu_chief_warrior,_2nd_century_BCE-1st_century_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
